;; Go's print level's divergences (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, REAP1, RPS3): the classes of the
;; non-passes of repr/go's round trips (bin/repr-go roundtrip, doc/go/ROUNDTRIP.md) for linux/amd64
;; (std and $GOROOT/test's programs, test/repr/go/roundtrip-linux-amd64.edn; the directory tests,
;; roundtrip-dirtest-linux-amd64.edn), of std with its tests (roundtrip-tests.edn with
;; roundtrip-tests-known.edn) and of the text level (mode :full, roundtrip-text-known.edn), in
;; test/goi/divergences.edn's format. A case is an entry whose levels do not all pass: "RESULT
;; LEVELS: the first line of the difference", RESULT the worst of fail, skip; or "known LEVELS:
;; reason" where its known file lists it. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :unsafe
  :title "unsafe has no export data or code"
  :kind :design
  :why "the package unsafe is the compiler's: its original does not compile, so the export and code levels are skip"
  :decided "doc/go/ROUNDTRIP.md, \"The corpus and the configuration\""
  :match [#"^skip export,code: original does not compile"]}
 {:id :compile-only-dirtests
  :title "directory tests that only compile: no run level"
  :kind :design
  :why "compiledir and builddir tests build no program to run against the golden output (Go's test driver's actions)"
  :decided "doc/go/ROUNDTRIP.md, \"Directory tests\"; test/repr/go/roundtrip-dirtest-known.edn"
  :match [#"^skip run: $"]}
 {:id :tests-embed-sources
  :title "TamaGo's tests embed their package's own sources"
  :kind :design
  :why "testdata_tamago_test.go files embed the package's Go files (//go:embed *.go): the candidate's sources compiled in the original's place embed the candidate's text, so a string symbol of the test binary differs, not the program's code"
  :decided "doc/go/ROUNDTRIP.md, \"Known gaps\"; test/repr/go/roundtrip-tests-known.edn"
  :match [#"^known code: .*embed"]}
 {:id :empty-decl-group
  :title "an empty declaration group (import ( ), a local var ())"
  :kind :design
  :why "it declares nothing and has no element in the forms (go/ast keeps the GenDecl; the converter writes its specs only)"
  :decided "doc/go/PRINTER-NOTES.md, G2F6 (the user, 2026-10-17); doc/go/SPEC.md §10.2"
  :match [#"^known text: (import \( \)|var \(\)) with no specs"]}
]
